+class_name VfxAura3D
+extends RefCounted
+## The 3D aura (docs/vfx/aura3d.md; Orb's direction 2026-10-18): a shader-driven shell round each fighter whose surface pulses, shimmers, froths and undulates, a different foundation for each fighter,
+## the Protagonist's and the Anti-hero's INVERTED rather than recoloured. Behind a switch (`hub.aura3d_enabled`, off by default: `hub.set_aura3d(true)` also turns the old standing aura off), so
+## nothing changes until it is turned on. Presentation only: it reads the standing aura's eased level (aura.gd), the fighter's tier and lane colour, and writes nothing.
+## The themes (every pair is an inversion; the numbers are in data/vfx/aura3d.json):
+##   protagonist, BOIL: a furnace giving heat away. Outward: the shell swells out and relaxes (an exhale, fast out, slow back); the skin froths with round bubbles that grow, ring and thin out
+##     (bright RINGS on a clear skin), drifting UP like convection; a soft rim; the froth gets coarser and quicker with the tier. Irregular, warm, spending itself.
+##   rival, FACETS: cold pride held in. Inward: the shell is smaller and draws in and holds (a smooth inhale); the skin is a lattice of crystal facets (bright FACETS between dark SEAMS: the boil's
+##     polarity inverted), each glinting in its own slow turn like frost, settling DOWN like cold air; a crisp rim; at tier 3 and up the seams are lit from inside (pride cracking). Ordered, still.
